    Order the flow parity test's setup before its non-blocking stream
    
    The Device helper zeroed and filled buffers with cudaMemset and pageable
    cudaMemcpy on the legacy stream, which a cudaStreamNonBlocking stream does
    not wait for. After the 4K case's 25 MB of setup the zeroing of the cell
    buffer landed after the kernel wrote it, so the s=2 comparison saw zeros
    (GPU (0,0) vs CPU (49.92, -53.27)); the kernels were correct. Synchronize
    the device after each setup call. 20/20 runs now pass at both 1920x1080
    and 3840x2160; without the change 20/20 fail.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JrVDhHj2LLgL7AQK1ynMV4

